* sim_unit.cir.in: the SCPA unit cell switching at 1 GHz from 1.2 V.
* A template: run_flow.sh replaces NETLIST and PINS to make two decks,
*   sim_ref.cir  from ref.spice            (schematic: no wiring, no parasitics)
*   sim_pex.cir  from scpa_unit_pex.spice  (the layout with its parasitic capacitance)
* The cap's top plate is held at 0 V, standing in for the PA's output node at AC ground.

* IHP's transistor (typical corner) and capacitor models
.lib /foss/pdks/ihp-sg13g2/libs.tech/ngspice/models/cornerMOSlv.lib mos_tt
.lib /foss/pdks/ihp-sg13g2/libs.tech/ngspice/models/cornerCAP.lib cap_typ
.include NETLIST

VDD vdd 0 1.2
* 1 GHz square wave: 0 to 1.2 V, 20 ps edges, 480 ps high, period 1 ns
VIN a 0 PULSE(0 1.2 0 20p 20p 480p 1n)
XU PINS scpa_unit

.control
tran 1p 6n
* Energy from the supply per cycle: average supply current x 1.2 V / 1 GHz.
* ngspice counts current into the source's + terminal as positive, so the supply's is negative.
meas tran iavg AVG i(VDD) from=2n to=6n
let e_fj = -iavg*1.2/1e9*1e15
print e_fj
* Delay: input falling through 0.6 V to the output rising through 0.6 V, third cycle.
meas tran tpd TRIG v(a) VAL=0.6 FALL=3 TARG v(xu.out) VAL=0.6 RISE=3
.endc
.end
